      "writtenOn": "2018-10-17T13:54:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This file is actually chip/arch specific, so it is okay to have raw assembly for this arch in this file.\n\nThere\u0027s no need to have inline assembly in a driver for a peripheral. If you want a nop instruction provide an inline function (lives in some header file) that has the semantics you desire. \n\nWhat is the reason for doing a pause here anyway? What are the expectations for status to be set accordingly. Also, I see a hard coded \u0027500\u0027 below. That is assuming quite a lot of things: ish core speed, execution timing of pause, and somehow that works out to 500? This is a brittle construct.\n\nAlso, why is\u0027rep nop\u0027 being employed instead of \u0027pause\u0027 ?",
      "parentUuid": "c8e389bd_465dd0ba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 336,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 336,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "695d3f214afde61c8e2b0ac2d0fec424223a8146",
